\{"kind":"table","sheet":"Table 1","address":"A3:F12","rows":10,"cols":6,"values":[["Immune Cell Type","Crosstalk with Gut Microbiota","Key Metabolites/Mechanisms","Functional Impact","Therapeutic Relevance","References"],["Macrophages","Bacteroides fragilis enhances phagocytic function via polysaccharide A (PSA).\\n\\nSCFAs (e.g., butyrate) reduce NF-kB signaling and promote anti-inflammatory M2 macrophages.\\n\\nLPS from Enterobacteriaceae induces pro-inflammatory M1 polarization.","SCFAs (butyrate, propionate), PSA, LPS","Balances inflammation; promotes tissue repair and pathogen clearance.","FMT to restore SCFA-producing taxa; engineered probiotics targeting M2 polarization.","[30, 90]"],["Dendritic Cells (DCs)","SFB (Segmented Filamentous Bacteria) induce Th17 differentiation via IL-23.\\n\\nLactobacillus spp. prime tolerogenic DCs through AhR ligands (e.g., indole derivatives).","AhR ligands (indole derivatives), flagellin","Enhances antigen presentation; balances Th17/Treg responses; maintains intestinal homeostasis.","AhR agonists (e.g., tryptophan metabolites); microbial consortia targeting DC maturation.","[28, 90]"],["NK Cells","Akkermansia muciniphila enhances NK cytotoxicity via TLR2 signaling.\\n\\nDysbiosis reduces NK cell-mediated tumor surveillance.","TLR2 ligands, SCFAs","Improves anti-tumor immunity; maintains mucosal barrier integrity.","Akkermansia supplementation; TLR2 agonists.","[91]"],["B Cells","Microbiota-driven IgA class-switching via Peyer's patches.\\n\\nBifidobacterium spp. promote IL-10+ regulatory B cells (Bregs).","IgA, polysaccharide A (PSA), SCFAs","Neutralizes pathobionts; reduces systemic autoimmunity; promotes gut homeostasis.","IgA-boosting probiotics; engineered IgA-coated microbes.","[92]"],["CD8+ T Cells","Butyrate inhibits HDACs, enhancing memory CD8+ T cell differentiation.\\n\\nDysbiosis exacerbates CD8+ exhaustion via PD-1 upregulation.","Butyrate, isoDCA, PD-1 ligands","Enhances anti-tumor cytotoxicity; mitigates exhaustion in chronic infections.","Butyrate supplements; PD-1/PD-L1 inhibitors.","[92, 93]"],["Th17 Cells","SFB and Citrobacter rodentium drive RORgt+ Th17 cells via IL-6/IL-23.\\n\\nSCFAs and lithocholic acid derivatives (e.g., 3-oxoLCA) suppress pathogenic Th17 differentiation by inhibiting RORgt activity.","SCFAs, 3-oxoLCA","Protects against fungal infections; exacerbates GVHD if dysregulated.","RORgt antagonists; SFB-targeted antibiotics.","[26, 27]"],["Treg Cells","Clostridia clusters produce butyrate, expanding colonic Foxp3+ Tregs.\\n\\nBacteroides fragilis PSA induces IL-10+ Tregs via TLR2.\\n\\nSecondary bile acids like isoalloLCA promote mitochondrial ROS for Foxp3 expression.\\n\\nDysbiosis and antibiotics reduce Treg numbers and alter their crosstalk with CD8 T cells, tipping balance toward GvHD.","Butyrate, PSA, isoalloLCA, SCFAs (butyrate), tryptophan catabolites, secondary bile acids.","Suppresses GVHD; maintains intestinal tolerance; enhances mucosal repair; suppress alloreactive CD8 T cell proliferation and tissue damage.","Postbiotics (e.g., butyrate analogs); FMT for Treg expansion; microbiome-preserving therapies may maintain Treg-CD8 balance.","[24, 25, 36]"],["ILC3s","Alistipes spp. activate AhR in ILC3s to produce IL-22.\\n\\nDysbiosis reduces ILC3-mediated epithelial repair and antimicrobial peptide production.","AhR ligands (indole derivatives), SCFAs","Enhances mucosal barrier repair; regulates lymphoid tissue development.","AhR agonists (e.g., dietary indoles); Alistipes consortia.","[31, 34]"],["gamma delta T Cells","Microbiota-derived D-lactate primes gamma delta T cells for IL-17 production.\\n\\nLactobacillus spp. modulate gamma delta T cell trafficking to gut mucosa through GPR15 signaling.","D-lactate, SCFAs","Early defense against pathogens; promotes tissue homeostasis.","D-lactate-producing probiotics; gamma delta T cell boosters.","[94]"]]\}\
